course: dictionary
lesson: 14035
title: A sign that shows
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A manifestation is a sign or a way that something shows itself. When an illness, a feeling or a problem becomes visible, we can say it has a manifestation. «Fever is a manifestation of illness» means a high temperature is a sign that the body is unwell.
explain: The word manifest means clear and easy to see, so a manifestation is something that makes an idea or a problem clear to see. «The rash on her arm was a manifestation of the allergy.» The rash is what you can see, and it shows the allergy is there.
explain: Look at the words around the word for clues. «The sneezing was an outward manifestation of her hay fever.» Outward means on the outside, where people can see it. So the sneezing is how the hay fever shows itself. Ask yourself: what is being shown?
explain: In stories, a manifestation can be a ghost or spirit that suddenly appears. «At midnight, a ghostly manifestation drifted along the corridor.» In church language, some believers call a sign of God's presence a manifestation. Epiphany, for example, is a feast that Christians celebrate as the manifestation of Jesus to the wise men.
fact: Manifestation is a noun. Its plural is manifestations.
fact: «Manifestation» means a sign or way that something shows itself.
fact: Phrases to know: «a manifestation of» something, «a physical manifestation», and «an outward manifestation».
fact: In stories, a manifestation can mean a ghost or spirit appearing.
fact: In religion, believers may call a sign of God's presence a manifestation, and Epiphany is described this way in church language.
exercise: «Fever is a manifestation of illness.» What does manifestation mean here? | *A sign that shows something is there | A doctor's bill | A kind of medicine | A cure that makes you well
exercise: «The sneezing was an outward manifestation of her hay fever.» What does outward suggest? | Something hidden deep inside | *Something you can see from the outside | Something very quiet | Something that happened long ago
exercise: «At midnight, a ghostly manifestation drifted along the corridor.» In this story, what does manifestation mean? | A long walk in the woods | *The appearance of a ghost | A loud noise from a radio | A kind of cake
test: «Dark clouds are a manifestation of the coming storm.» What does manifestation mean? | A sudden silence | A kind of weather map | A cloud shaped like a dog | *A sign that something is coming
test: «Christians believe Epiphany is the manifestation of Jesus to the wise men.» What does manifestation mean here? | A type of church song | A party with lots of food | A long journey to a faraway country | *The showing of something holy, as believers see it
exam: «The boy's anger was a manifestation of his worry about the test.» What does manifestation mean? | A sudden rainstorm | *A sign or way that the worry shows itself | A hidden treasure in a box | Being very tired after school
